{
  "id": "V17",
  "title": "Deflection distribution — closed form and a starved stacked wall (F-DD1)",
  "intent": "Line A: two walls (6 ft and 12 ft) share the story shear by stiffness, k = V/δ from SDPWS Eq. 4.3-1, iterated until the wall δ are within 5 %. With linear δ (no plate crushing beyond r = 0.73, fixed hardware) the converged split has a closed form, which is checked here. Line B (finding F-DD1, pinned design): a 4 ft Level 1 wall (SW-6) under a 4 ft wall (SW-4). The δ of SW-6 includes the holdown slip and crushing from the end force SW-4 sends down, which does not depend on the own share of SW-6 — an offset. Equal δ at Level 1 then gives SW-6 only a few percent of the story shear (starved), although its capacity share is about a third. The tool converges to that split; this case fixes the numbers for the F-DD1 solver work.",
  "covers": [
    "Deflection distribution (k = V/δ, 5 % spread, 20 passes)",
    "SDPWS Eq. 4.3-1",
    "Stacked walls: offset from the forces above (F-DD1)"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Line A, both walls 6\" o.c. (G_a = 16 k/in), HDUE3 (δ 0.127 in at 3790 lb), (2)2x4 end posts (A = 10.5 in²), h = 10 ft. δ per kip of wall shear: c = 8,000,000/(E·A·L²) + h/(L·G_a) + (h/L)·[0.127·(1000h/L)/3790 + 0.02·(1000h/L)/(A·625)/0.73]."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "SW-1 (L = 6): c_1 = 0.0124 + 0.1042 + 0.1047 = 0.2213 in/k → k_1 = 4.519 k/in. SW-2 (L = 12): c_2 = 0.0031 + 0.0521 + 0.0262 = 0.0814 in/k → k_2 = 12.290 k/in."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "Converged split V_i = V·k_i/Σk: V_1 = 6 × 4.519/16.809 = 1.613 k, V_2 = 4.387 k (by length it would be 2.00 / 4.00 k — the long wall is stiffer than its length share)."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "Every wall deflects δ = V/Σk = 6/16.809 = 0.3569 in → spread 0 (well inside 5 %). Stiffness reported as k = V·1000/δ: 4519 and 12290 lb/in."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "Check the assumptions: v = 188.18 / 255.91 plf ≤ 312 → 6\" o.c. on both; SW-2 T = 0.7 × 4.387 × 10/12 − 0.46 × 0.60 = 2.283 k ≤ 3.79 → HDUE3; crushing r = 0.410 / 0.557 < 0.73 → linear."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "Line B: 2nd story SW-3 (8 ft) and SW-4 (4 ft) over SW-5 (8 ft) / SW-6 (4 ft), all 2\" o.c. both sides (G_a = 56); 1.0E = 7 k at Level 2 only, so both stories carry 7 k. Pinned: SW-3 MSTC66 + (3)2x4, SW-4 MSTC40 + (2)2x4, SW-5 HDUE13 + 8x4, SW-6 HDUE3 + (2)2x4. δ(V, T_above) = 8vh³/(EAb) + vh/(1000G_a) + (h/b)·[δ_cap·T/P_δ + Δ_c(r)], T = 1000·V·h/L + T_above (MSTC P_δ = cap/0.7, HDUE P_δ = cap)."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "Level 2 (nothing above): equal δ → V_3 = 5.670 k, V_4 = 1.330 k, δ = 0.3151 in at both walls. The 1.0E end forces sent down: SW-3 T = 7088 lb onto SW-5, SW-4 T = 3324 lb onto SW-6."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Level 1 offsets: SW-6 at zero own share already deflects d_6 = δ(0, 3324 lb) = 0.3132 in (its HDUE3 slip and crushing under the force from SW-4, × h/b = 2.5). SW-5 carrying the whole 7 k deflects 0.4443 in > d_6, so an equal-δ split exists."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "Level 1 equal δ: V_6 = 0.367 k (5.24 % of the story), V_5 = 6.633 k, δ = 0.4261 in. By capacity SW-6 would take 31.91 % (2.23 k): the stack above starves it (finding F-DD1)."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "text": "Offset check (note in G3): δ_6(0)/δ = 0.3132 / 0.4261 = 0.73 > 0.5 → SW-6 is noted: most of its deflection comes from the force of SW-4 above; δ_5(0)/δ = 0.1140 / 0.4261 = 0.27 → no note."
    },
    {
      "step": 11,
      "text": "Line A drift (Cd 4, Ie 1.0, RC II): the two walls give the same δ at their shares (0.3569 in), so δxe = the story δ and either wall can be named as governing. Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-2 0.3569 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.3569 / 1.0 = 1.428 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in → OK."
    },
    {
      "step": 12,
      "text": "Line B drift: Level 2 δ = 0.3151 in, Level 1 δ = 0.4261 in (equal δ at each story, end forces from above included). Story drift Level 2: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-4 0.3151 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.3151 / 1.0 = 1.260 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in → OK. Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-6 0.4261 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.4261 / 1.0 = 1.704 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in → OK."
    }
  ],
